Date: Thu, 16 Apr 1998 16:46:21 -0400
Subject: Re: [S] Plot with confidence interval
Message-ID: <9804161646.ZM16304@pascal.math.yorku.ca>

>
>      Does anyone have a function to plot means and confidence intervals
> by group. 
>

The following is a simple way of getting a display of means +/- 2 SEs.

Suppose "y" contains the data, and "group", the grouping factor. Then

        > plot.gam ( lm(y~-1+group) , se= T)

will do the trick.  With a larger model, plot.gam will show adjusted
means and "adjusted data" (with residuals=T).

