From daryl.b.lambert at intel.com  Fri Apr 17 01:15:00 1998
From: daryl.b.lambert at intel.com (Lambert, Daryl B)
Date: Thu, 16 Apr 1998 18:15:00 -0700
Subject: RE: [S] Plot with confidence interval
Message-ID: <199804171847.LAA11322@hebe.or.intel.com>

     
     One way to skin this cat-
     
     Get your data into a format like so:
     
         group subgroup    foo 
      1 group1        a   60.4
      2 group1        a  219.7
      3 group1        a   91.4
      4 group1        b   17.3
      5 group1        b   81.1
      6 group1        b   97.6
      7 group1        c -103.9
      8 group1        c   -2.1
      9 group1        c  157.7
     10 group2        a    1.4
     11 group2        a  156.3
     12 group2        a  167.6
     13 group2        b  -23.4
     14 group2        b  -96.1
     15 group2        b  -56.6
     16 group2        c  -34.3
     17 group2        c    4.7
     18 group2        c   41.1
     
     Then try this:
     
 
dotplot(subgroup~foo|group,data=groupdata,layout=c(1,2,1),groups=subgr
     oup,panel=panel.superpose))
     
     The axes are flipped from your example, and you would have to edit 
     panel.dotplot to draw the lines between points if you really want 
     them.  But the right information, grouping, and symbol coding are 
     done.
     
     Daryl
     daryl.b.lambert at intel.com

